`nix/uclibc-legacy.patch` contains uClibc-ng library changes and context
under the upstream LGPL-2.1-or-later terms (COPYING.LIB).
`nix/uclibc-thread-probe.patch` retains the LinuxThreads LGPL-2.0-or-later terms.
These dependency patches do not change the agent's license. Corresponding
library source and these patches must remain available when redistributing
the legacy linked executable.

Project design notes live under design/. System Jansson and system libcurl are
build/runtime dependencies; no third-party
Jansson or libcurl implementation source or upstream header source is vendored.
`src/snag_jansson_abi.h` is a GPL-2.0-only first-party declaration shim for
minimal build roots that provide the Jansson runtime library without the
development header; it contains no third-party implementation code and is
inventoried by `make depscheck`. `make depclosurecheck` captures and validates
the current-host dynamic executable closure, and `make evidencebundle`/
`make evidencecheck` provide a machine-readable release-evidence record. A
release follows RELEASE.md: every implemented target ships with matching
source, licenses, symbols and checksums, with its actual platform/testing scope.
Optional historical evidence bundles do not replace that production matrix or
turn experimental cross-builds into runtime-qualified platforms.
